# Untyped CSV streaming over a multi-buffer mixed file

Measures lazy untyped row streaming for 100,000 mixed rows in a multi-megabyte
file. Cells include integer-looking, text, boolean-looking, and decimal-looking
values; the loop counts rows without materializing the source.

>>> prepare
python generate_data.py

>>> checkpoint lazy-csv 4789cddab3297ac9753fc94e0c4e64ca739b1c2f First buildable commit after lazy streaming CSV

>>> source
use CSV

let source = CSV.read("data/large_mixed.csv")
let rows = 0
for (row in source) {
    rows = rows + 1
}
print(rows)
